course: dictionary
lesson: 14682
title: One word, many meanings: pressed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Pressed is the past form of press, so it tells us something already happened: «Sam pressed the lift button.» Press means to push firmly on something.
explain: One word can have several meanings, so use the context to choose. A button is pressed by pushing it. Flowers are pressed by flattening them between pages. Clothes are pressed when an iron makes them smooth. «Pressed for time» is different again: it means having very little time.
explain: Check your choice by putting your meaning into the sentence. «The pressed leaves were flat and dry in her book.» Does «flattened to dry» make sense there? Yes, so that is the right meaning.
fact: Pressed means pushed on something, like a button or a key.
fact: «Pressed» flowers and leaves are flattened between pages to dry and keep.
fact: «Pressed» clothes are made smooth with an iron.
fact: «Pressed for time» means having very little time.
fact: The sentence around a word tells you which meaning is the right one.
exercise: «Mia pressed the doorbell twice.» What does pressed mean here? | Flattened to dry | Made smooth with an iron | *Pushed on | Having very little time
exercise: «Dad pressed his shirt before the party.» What does pressed mean here? | Short of time | Pushed a button | Dried between the pages of a book | *Made smooth with an iron
exercise: You press the button at the crossing. What should you do next? | Close your eyes and count to ten | *Wait for the green figure | Run straight across the road | Shout for help
test: The total starts at 0. Each time the key is pressed, add 2. How many presses make a total of 8? | 6 | 3 | 5 | *4
test: «Lena pressed daisies in a book to keep them.» What does pressed mean here? | Made smooth with an iron | *Flattened to dry and keep | Pushed on a key | Very short of time
exam: Jo was «pressed for time» before school. What does that mean? | Was pushed on the back | Had plenty of time to spare | Had a flower pressed in her book | *Had very little time
